> My question is a rough outline of how to proceed, should I go for the
> mines? should I do Sokoban?

Wha'ts your AC? A low AC is your top priority at this stage of the
game. Try to get it below zero, or at least below 3 or 4. Look for
(studded) leather armour, gloves, boots, wizard hats and leather hats.
Keep an eye out for metal helms too, they might be helms of brilliance,
which are great for wizards. If you can wear it without being burdened,
crystal armour is also good. Beware of trying on armour that might turn
out to be cursed though. An altar can help you with this, or careful
price-IDing in a shop, or if you have IDed ?oDestroy Armour, each one
of those will let you 'remove' one item that turns out to be cursed.

> I am afraid of levelling up to much because
> If I understand it correctly the Monster generation is relative to your
> charecter level.

yes, this is true, but levelling up too high isn't (necessarily) the
end of the world. You're probably safe to gain another level or two. It
depends on your circumstances.

With a ring of slow digestion, you an afford to play very slowly and
cautiously. What kills a lot of early wizards is the pressure to
explore deeper and deeper in search of food. Get yourself a stash with
a chest or box, preferably by an altar, and return to it often. Clear a
level, return to stash to ID, sort and use your loot. Clear another
level, return to stash. When a better site for your stash turns up,
move it, making lots of trips and make good use of the Bag of Holding
you (might) find in soko to avoid being burdened.

It depends on your kit, your stats and your spells, but in your
position I would probably proceed carefully into the mines. If the
first level is unlit, then make that *very* carefully. A good strategy
is to hang around the stairs, killing gnomes and dwarves a few at a
time, then retreating to recover before taking on some more.

If you haven't found an altar in the main dungeon yet, the minetown
temple will be very useful to you (especially if co-aligned), for IDing
items and donating for priest protection. The shops can be handy as
well. There's little point going beyond minetown before doing soko
though.

> P.S. Pretty Kitty was killed by a rock trap :(

If you get the chance, replace her. Pets are important for early
wizards, particularly if you're concerned about levelling up too
quickly. You can tame dogs and cats with tripe or food rations.
Normally I would consider this a waste of precious food for a young
wiz, but with your ring it's not so bad. Just keep eating corpses
(except when satiated) and try to keep at least one decent snack handy
for yourself at all times, just in case. You can find lots of food in
soko.

Finally, watch out for bones files! They can be very dangerous. If you
encounter one, proceed with caution or, better yet, retreat to your
stash and come back later.



